From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AgentLand <agentland@localhost>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:17:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] EndpointBuilder: no panics, and a refused address keeps
 the builder

bind_addr took the builder out of its mutex and returned early when
iroh refused the address (a second IPv4 address, for example), so the
builder was gone. Every later call then panicked on "EndpointBuilder
consumed" while holding the mutex, and after that on the poisoned
mutex; calls after bind() panicked the same way. A panic through the
FFI ends the foreign process.

- Bind addresses are checked on a scratch builder when they are set
  and applied to the real builder when it binds, so a refused address
  leaves the builder as it was.
- map() returns an error instead of expect(); methods that return a
  Result fail with "EndpointBuilder was already used by bind()", and
  the ones without an error in their FFI signature (apply_*, alpns,
  relay_mode) do nothing and log a warning: no endpoint can be made
  from a used builder.
- A poisoned mutex is recovered instead of unwrapped.

